a cooler airport) can hide or exaggerate a long-run trend, so the recent decades are the clearer guide here.","t_mon":"Lows rose in none. Highs rose in 7 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Columbus has gotten wetter","p_rain":"Columbus' yearly precipitation has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.45 inches per decade</strong> (95% range +0.21 to +0.69), about +6.5 inches since 1879. The 1991\u20132020 normal is 41.5 inches a year. The wettest year was 2018 (55.18 in); the driest, 1930 (21.60 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":true,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 5 daily record highs, 1 daily record low"}}